{% from "macros.njk" import callout, snippet with context %}

{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Cards group related content and its actions on a single bordered surface.
     In the M2 2020 style they are quiet: a 1px border does the separation
     work that a shadow would do elsewhere, so cards read as *containers*,
     not as floating layers.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Content pieces are <strong>heterogeneous</strong> — a title, a
        paragraph, actions, maybe a nested detail — that belong together.</li>
    <li>You need scrollable feed content (the mail-style timeline in the
        demos: section label, then a stack of cards).</li>
    <li>The card hosts a self-contained interaction (a notification with
        Dismiss/Upgrade actions).</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Items are <strong>peers of the same structure</strong> — that is a
        <a href="lists.html">list</a>, not a card stack; rows are lighter and
        denser.</li>
    <li>You need a modal surface — the dialog (planned 0.4) over the scrim is
        that, not a positioned card.</li>
    <li>Everything on the page would be a card — borders everywhere is visual
        noise; let section labels and spacing carry quiet groupings.</li>
  </ul>
  {{ callout({
    variant: "info",
    title: "Card vs. list row",
    text: "Cards for varied, self-contained content. Lists for repeated, peer items. The demos mix them: card stacks in the feed, list rows in the inbox.",
    href: "lists.html",
    linkText: "Lists"
  }) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-anatomy">Anatomy</h2>
  <div class="docs-anatomy">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 240" role="img" aria-label="Card anatomy diagram">
      <!-- card -->
      <rect x="40" y="24" width="380" height="190" rx="8" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <!-- title -->
      <rect x="64" y="48" width="180" height="12" rx="6" fill="#444746"/>
      <!-- text -->
      <rect x="64" y="76" width="320" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <rect x="64" y="92" width="290" height="8" rx="4" fill="#9aa0a6"/>
      <!-- action row -->
      <rect x="230" y="168" width="54" height="8" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <rect x="300" y="160" width="96" height="26" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <!-- border callout -->
      <line x1="40" y1="230" x2="420" y2="230" stroke="#1a73e8" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <!-- second card below, gap indicator -->
      <rect x="40" y="236" width="380" height="4" fill="none"/>
      <!-- callout numbers -->
      <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
        <g><circle cx="40" cy="24" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="40" y="28" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="64" cy="48" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="64" y="52" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="64" cy="80" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="64" y="84" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="348" cy="173" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="348" y="177" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Surface</strong> — white, 1px <code>--fl-border</code>, 8px radius (<code>--fl-radius-card</code>), 16px padding. Never a shadow.</li>
      <li><strong>Title</strong> — 16px/500 (<code>--fl-fs-title</code>), the card's <code>h2</code>–<code>h4</code> level.</li>
      <li><strong>Text</strong> — 14px body in secondary color.</li>
      <li><strong>Action row (optional)</strong> — text button left of the filled one, right-aligned; mirrors the auth-card convention.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stacking:</strong> adjacent cards get a 16px gap automatically (<code>.fl-card + .fl-card</code>) — wrap a feed in a container and the rhythm is free.</li>
    <li><strong>Grouping:</strong> <code>fl-section-label</code> (uppercase caption) heads each group; it collapses its top margin as the first child of a container.</li>
    <li><strong>Cards are not interactive surfaces by default</strong> — no hover fill, no cursor change. Interactivity belongs to the controls inside. Whole-clickable cards are not in the library (planned pattern: make an inner link cover the card).</li>
    <li><strong>Composition:</strong> cards nest (the demos show a button row inside a card) and work with every shell's <code>fl-content</code> column, capped at <code>--fl-content-max</code> on desktop.</li>
    <li><strong>Width:</strong> block-level, fills its container — constrain the parent, don't set card widths.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use a real heading element for <code>fl-card__title</code> and keep the page's heading order sane (cards are usually <code>h2</code>/<code>h3</code>, never skip levels for styling).</li>
    <li><code>&lt;article class="fl-card"&gt;</code> gives each card its own landmark-ish region in feed contexts (screen readers list the articles).</li>
    <li>Action rows keep real buttons — same rules as the buttons page; right-aligned text-then-filled order preserves a logical focus order.</li>
    <li>The border/separation is presentation, not semantics — no <code>role</code> needed on the card itself.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

